00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:57.000
Elizabeth and her companion Bill Wallace witnessed a dishevelled man behaving suspiciously along the shoreline before driving off from the beach car park in a dusty white station wagon at around 3pm. Elizabeth and Bill tailed the vehicle to Noosa Junction, where they lost sight of it driving towards Pinaroo Park. After hearing about Sharn Kingi's disappearance, Elizabeth reported this information to police and investigators subsequently reached out to Bill Wallace for further information. Bill's description of both the man and the station wagon matched perfectly with the information police had already obtained from Elizabeth and other witnesses,

