That evening, 18-year-old Neil Clark was walking home from his fruit-picking job through Timbierre Mountain State Forest, located 17 kilometres south of Newster. As he trekked along the edge of the overgrown forest of eucalyptus trees and rainforest ferns, Neil was struck by a foul stench. He decided that if the odor was still there the next morning, he would have a look around to investigate its source. At 8.50am the following morning of Thursday, December 3, Neil Clark drove his car to the area of forest where he had picked up the offensive odor the previous day. The smell was still lingering in the crisp mountain air, so Neil followed the scent, stepping off the track and venturing a short way into the forest towards Castaway's creek.

