clothing style so they wouldn't match any descriptions provided by potential witnesses and washed their car thoroughly inside and out to remove any evidence. Watts continued to reassure Beck that he didn't feel bad about the crime and neither should she. As the week wore on, Sean Kingey's disappearance remained a mystery to police and the killer couple started to relax. It wasn't until they heard news that Sean's body had been found and police were interested in speaking to the owner of a white station wagon that the pair became spooked. Watts and Beck hastily packed suitcases, got in their car and left Lowwood. They headed interstate towards Victoria, where they figured they would be able to

