information in relation to the disappearance of Helen Feeney, but subsequent questioning proved fruitless and led to no breakthroughs in the case. By 2008, Velmae Beck had a number of severe health problems. After being hospitalized for minor heart surgery in May that year, Beck's condition deteriorated and she was put into an induced coma. Detectives remained convinced that Beck knew more about other crimes than she ever admitted and held out hopes for a deathbed confession. There was heated debate about whether Beck, who had expressed the desire not to be resuscitated, should be kept alive for that reason. On May 27, 2008, 64-year-old Velmae Beck died in custody at Townsville Hospital from complications arising from heart surgery. Investigators never got their

